---
// Practitioner deep-dive — rendered only in pro state (door 3). The whole block
// is wrapped in .wn-pro, so it's hidden for everyone else. Content is drawn from
// Part Two of the SVH document: co-regulation, connected-and-soft vs catharsis,
// the Cup, oscillation & pendulation, and the no-healer stance.
---

<div class="wn-pro">
  <!-- Holding space — co-regulation band (svhgpt-06) -->
  <section class="wn-band wn-band--tall">
    <div class="wn-band-bg" data-parallax data-parallax-speed="0.2" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/media/library/svhgpt-06-holding-space.webp" alt="" />
    </div>
    <div class="wn-band-inner">
      <p class="wn-band-quote wn-reveal">
        Healing can <em>come through</em> —<br />not you healing someone.
      </p>
      <div class="wn-band-by wn-reveal">The no-healer stance · the practitioner holds space</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wn-practice">
    <div class="wn-practice-inner">
      <div class="wn-practice-head wn-reveal">
        <div class="we-eyebrow">If you come from somatic work</div>
        <h2 class="we-h2">You already carry the map.<br /><em>Here's where the voice fits.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="wn-practice-grid">
        <article class="wn-practice-card wn-reveal">
          <i class="ph-light ph-heartbeat ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h4>Connected and soft — <em>not catharsis</em></h4>
          <p>
            Screaming into a pillow lives "in the house of the sympathetic nervous
            system." It discharges, but it rehearses the very reaction. Here you
            stay ventral — shoulders soft, jaw soft — and put the charge into the
            <strong>tone</strong>. <em>"You're not embodying it — you're going to put it
            in the tone."</em>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="wn-practice-card wn-reveal" style="--wn-delay: 90ms">
          <i class="ph-light ph-arrows-clockwise ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h4>The <em>change of context</em></h4>
          <p>
            Originally survival demanded fight or freeze. In a session the body
            re-learns: <em>"I can access this energy without my whole nervous system
            going into that state. It is safe to go here while staying connected
            and soft."</em> That re-learning is what makes room for healing.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="wn-practice-card wn-reveal" style="--wn-delay: 180ms">
          <i class="ph-light ph-waveform ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h4>Oscillation &amp; <em>pendulation</em></h4>
          <p>
            <strong>Oscillation</strong> is the rhythm of the whole arc you design —
            activation then regulation, depth then integration.
            <strong>Pendulation</strong> is the in-the-moment move: toward the
            difficult, then deliberately back to something safe, then back again.
            Both keep the system inside its window of tolerance.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="wn-practice-card wn-reveal" style="--wn-delay: 270ms">
          <i class="ph-light ph-hand-heart ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h4>Attunement over <em>protocol</em></h4>
          <p>
            The shift most protocol-trained practitioners make is toward the
            <strong>Cup</strong> — empty, cupped hands receiving the next step. You
            hold plans lightly and let the cup fill one move at a time.
            Information is <em>received</em>, not grabbed.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Cup, featured (svhgpt-05) -->
  <section class="wn-deeper" style="background: var(--paper-soft);">
    <div class="wn-deeper-inner">
      <div class="wn-deeper-media wn-reveal" data-parallax data-parallax-speed="0.15">
        <img src="/media/library/svhgpt-05-the-cup-receiving.webp" alt="Two cupped hands cradling a small ember of light" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="wn-deeper-text wn-reveal">
        <div class="we-eyebrow">The Cup</div>
        <h2 class="wn-deeper-h2">You don't need the whole arc — <em>only the next move.</em></h2>
        <p>
          The cup works at the level of intuition, <em>beyond right and wrong.</em>
          The impulse that lands can be trusted — but its <strong>translation</strong>
          through your trained mind is fallible. So pause and ask whether the
          first interpretation is the only one, rather than racing down a familiar
          pathway.
        </p>
        <p>
          And when sounding alone can't carry someone across a large bridge, SVH
          uses a constellation-style form — <em>Klankopstellingen</em> — that gives
          feelings and parts their right place, with the voice woven through.
        </p>
        <p class="wn-deeper-pull">
          The same disciplines you know — window of tolerance, dosage, oscillation.
          What diverges: the <em>voice as the primary channel,</em> and acknowledgment
          over discharge.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
